Subject: register VM: inline the frame release into the return path

What this does:
  regvm_record_release is marked always_inline, so the two callers that walk a
  finished frame -- regvm_t_return_nested, the hot return, and the other
  release site -- no longer pay a call/ret pair for every return. The
  var_ref arm, which only runs when the frame actually closed a closure, is
  inlined with the rest and becomes part of the return handler's cold tail.

Why we need it:
  The return path is the tail of every call. At 10.6 M calls per box2d run the
  call/ret pair is real work in a function that is otherwise a short walk over
  about ten registers.

Adds:
  * quickjs.c: the forward declaration and the definition of
    regvm_record_release gain __attribute__((always_inline)) inline.

Evidence:
  box2d fixed.js, clang-19 -O3, perf stat -r7: 29.198 G to 29.167 G
  instructions (-0.11%, -31 M), cycles -0.29%, wall -0.28%. The call micros
  drop 3.0 instructions per call (call.js 355.0 to 352.0, meth.js 488.0 to
  485.0). objdump: regvm_t_return_nested 35 to 131 instructions of code (the
  inlined cold arm) and the regvm_record_release symbol is gone.
  Box2d checksum 546.1008391043414 is unchanged and the register differential
  suite is 398/0/0 in both mono and threaded modes; a -DQJS_REGVM_VERIFY=1 -O1
  build is clean and prints the same checksum.

  This is the only part of the plan's X5 call-protocol item that measured a
  real reduction. The three other shapes tried there -- replacing the register
  memset with an unrolled undefined-store loop, coalescing JSRegRun's
  constant-zero clears, and merging the regs and var_refs clears -- all raised
  instruction counts and were reverted. The remaining ~90 instructions per
  call need a stack-allocated typed-register frame, not more hoisting.

Bytecode bump:
  No. No opcode, operand encoding or frame layout changes.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -23769,7 +23769,8 @@
